  "chapter": {
    "number": 146,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(147) Alleluia, a Psalm of Aggaeus and Zacharias."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Praise you⌃ the Lord: for psalmody is a good thing; let praise be sweetly sung to our God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord builds up Jerusalem; and he will gather together the dispersed of Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He heals the broken in heart, and binds up their wounds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He numbers the multitudes of stars; and calls them all by names.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Great is our Lord, and great is his strength; and his understanding is infinite.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord lifts up the meek; but brings sinners down to the ground.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Begin the song with thanksgiving to the Lord; sing praises on the harp to our God:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who covers the heaven with clouds, who prepares rain for the earth, who causes grass to spring up on the mountains, [",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 264
          },
          {
            "text": "and green herb for the service of men;]",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and gives cattle their food, and to the young ravens that call upon him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He will not take pleasure in the strength of a horse; neither is he well-pleased with the legs of a man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord takes pleasure in them that fear him, and in all that hope in his mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 264,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "See Ps 103 (104) 14.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 146,
          "verse": 8
        }
      }
    ]
